{
  "spec": "LXMF-rust/DISPLAY_NAMES.md section 3 (cleaning), 2.1 (the name: key 0 of the Retichat field 0xD1, a map), 4.1 (digest)",
  "notes": [
    "input_hex / fields_msgpack_hex are raw bytes as lowercase hex.",
    "expected is the cleaned name as a JSON string, or null for None.",
    "clean_announce applies clean() and then maps 'Anonymous Peer' (ASCII case-insensitive) to None.",
    "decode_field: the name is key 0 of the map at field 0xD1 ({0xD1: {0: name}}); a 0xD1 that is not a map is absent. state is absent | clear | name; display_name is set only for state name. More Retichat-field cases (group entries) are in retichat_field_vectors.json.",
    "digest_hex is the first 16 bytes of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 of input.",
    "Interpretation of rule 5: after truncation, trailing U+0020 and U+200D are stripped repeatedly (see the 'trailing' vectors).",
    "Order of rules 2 and 3: U+0085 is White_Space, so rule 2 turns it into a space before rule 3 could remove it as C1."
  ],
